nom is 27 C, m=1, the control of m3 (27 C, m=3) and of off (80 C, m=3); every deck gives tc1 and tc2 (instance on the
value forms, model on the geometry forms); geometry: rsh, narrow, short, l, w (r); cj, cjsw, narrow, short, w, l (c);
csect, length, mu, nt (l). i(vd) for r_*, |i(vd)| at 1 MHz for c_* and l_* (an inductor behind 1 ohm).
Oracle (fd.py, last lines): the multiplier's metamorphic relation, every m3 reading 3 times its nom reading within
1e-9 relative and 1e-10 absolute; a failing row is printed.
Both simulators shorten and narrow a resistor by twice short and narrow (r_geometry_nom: 100*(10u-0.4u)/(2u-0.2u)
= 533.3 ohm). The l_* decks do not hold the m relation (the 1-ohm resistor is not multiplied); both read the same.
Result: no difference.
Rechecked 2026-11-13 under R91b (../../checked.sh: a run whose exit status is not 0 or whose output says it aborted, stepped too small or met a singular matrix gives refused(<why>), never a reading): every reading reproduced.

